<title>UK: ABN AMRO unit sets $200 mln bond due December 1998.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO unit sets $200 mln bond due December 1998.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager ABN AMRO Hoare Govett.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ABN AMRO AUSTRALIA</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  ABN AMRO BANK NV</p>
<p> AMT	  $200 MLN  COUPON     6.50	MATURITY    30.DEC.98</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.915   PAY DATE    03.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.125     REOFFER    99.915    SPREAD	+8 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	**	  LISTING    AMSTERDAM PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  **	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/AU</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    DUTCH     HOME CTRY  NETHS     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  1.00	PRAECIP     NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.125 PCT U.S. TREASURY NOTE DUE 31.AUG.98</p>
<p> NOTES    **GUARANTOR RATED AA1/AA.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
